log_send_swallowed_error.s:
Make /api/send 503s diagnosable: today the real failure is swallowed. src/routes/api/send/+server.ts wraps both write calls in `.catch(() => { throw error(503, 'not_stored'); })` — group at lines 62-66, 1:1 at lines 119-121. Any rejection inside send_msg/send_group_msg (Qdrant HTTP error, or encrypt_text's importKey DataError) becomes a bare 503 'not_stored' with the ORIGINAL exception never logged, so the Cloudflare dashboard shows only the 503 and no cause. This is why the earlier x2-ws log dump looked healthy while the send died.

Change BOTH catch blocks to log the underlying error before rethrowing. Group (current lines 62-66):
```ts
		const m = await send_group_msg(
			env, me.id, group, text, image, file, reply_to, sticker, forwarded
		).catch(() => {
			throw error(503, 'not_stored');
		});
```
becomes:
```ts
		const m = await send_group_msg(
			env, me.id, group, text, image, file, reply_to, sticker, forwarded
		).catch((e) => {
			console.error('[SEND] not_stored', e);
			throw error(503, 'not_stored');
		});
```
1:1 (current lines 119-121):
```ts
	const m = await send_msg(env, me.id, to, text, image, file, reply_to, sticker, forwarded).catch(() => {
		throw error(503, 'not_stored');
	});
```
becomes:
```ts
	const m = await send_msg(env, me.id, to, text, image, file, reply_to, sticker, forwarded).catch((e) => {
		console.error('[SEND] not_stored', e);
		throw error(503, 'not_stored');
	});
```

Why over alternatives: console.error (not console.warn) so the prod log stream/observability surfaces it; keep status 503 so the client contract is unchanged; keep the catch inside the await so the send still rejects (never a lying ok:true).

Phase 1 tests first (src/routes/api/send/__tests__/server.test.ts, existing describe block 'POST /api/send — a failed write is surfaced, not silently 200d' lines 191-203): add, to each of the two existing 503 tests, a console.error spy assertion:
```ts
	it('503s a 1:1 send when send_msg rejects, instead of lying with ok: true', async () => {
		const err = new Error('qdrant down');
		sendMsgMock.mockRejectedValue(err);
		const spy = vi.spyOn(console, 'error').mockImplementation(() => {});
		await expect(POST(event({ to: 'bob', text: 'hi' }))).rejects.toMatchObject({ status: 503 });
		expect(spy).toHaveBeenCalledWith('[SEND] not_stored', err);
		spy.mockRestore();
	});
```
and the mirror for the group test with sendGroupMsgMock and event({ group: 'g1', text: 'hi' }). Use vi.spyOn(...).mockImplementation(() => {}) and spy.mockRestore() in the test body so stray logs don't pollute the run; vi.clearAllMocks() in beforeEach does NOT clear spyOn spies, hence explicit restore.

Phase 2: watch the new assertions fail for the stated reason (spy not called with err — current code logs nothing). Phase 3: implement the two catch-block edits above. Phase 4: `pnpm vitest run src/routes/api/send/__tests__/server.test.ts` green, then the full gate `pnpm test`. Note the 503 tests call POST directly (no RequestHandler wrapper) so console.error must be spied BEFORE the await — the handler runs synchronously inside the reject.

fail_loud_on_empty_enc_key.s:
Give the encryption failure a name so the dashboard log from step 1 shows the actual cause instead of a cryptic WebCrypto DataError. src/lib/server/msg_crypto.ts aes_key (lines 5-11) currently does `const raw = await get_secret(env.MESSAGE_ENC_KEY);` then `atob(raw)` → `Uint8Array.from('')` → `crypto.subtle.importKey('raw', [], 'AES-GCM', ...)` which throws a generic DataError with no mention of MESSAGE_ENC_KEY. Root cause of the prod outage: MESSAGE_ENC_KEY is referenced only in code (msg_crypto.ts:7, qdrant.ts:66); it is in NO wrangler.jsonc, NO .env, and the Secrets Store 45748cb1c67946df943075fa14cb8815 holds only TURN_KEY_API_TOKEN/TURN_KEY_ID/X2_ORIGIN. So get_secret (qdrant.ts:10-20) returns '' → importKey throws → encrypt_text throws → send_msg rejects → 503. Commit d3ccecd 'add_message_at_rest_encryption' documented this exact failure: 'without it encrypt_text's importKey throws, so /api/send degrades loudly'.

Change aes_key (msg_crypto.ts:5-11):
```ts
async function aes_key(env: QEnv & { MESSAGE_ENC_KEY?: SecretVal }): Promise<CryptoKey> {
	if (cached) return cached;
	const raw = await get_secret(env.MESSAGE_ENC_KEY);
	if (!raw) throw new Error('MESSAGE_ENC_KEY unset — cannot encrypt message text');
	const bytes = Uint8Array.from(atob(raw), (c) => c.charCodeAt(0));
	cached = await crypto.subtle.importKey('raw', bytes, 'AES-GCM', false, ['encrypt', 'decrypt']);
	return cached;
}
```
Also add a reset helper so tests can run the unset case after a valid key has already populated the module singleton (mirror qdrant.ts __reset_qdrant idiom):
```ts
export function __reset_msg_crypto(): void {
	cached = null;
}
```
Why: importKey on a 0-length key throws an opaque DataError; a named error carrying MESSAGE_ENC_KEY is greppable in dashboards. decrypt_text keeps its try/catch (msg_crypto.ts:38-40) which returns the stored ciphertext unchanged on any failure — that legacy-plaintext pass-through and the ciphertext-fallback both still hold, so reads never break.

Phase 1 tests first (src/lib/server/__tests__/msg_crypto.test.ts): add a `beforeEach(() => __reset_msg_crypto());` (import it) so the cache can't mask the unset case, then:
```ts
	it('throws a named error when MESSAGE_ENC_KEY is unset', async () => {
		await expect(encrypt_text({} as never, 'secret')).rejects.toThrow(/MESSAGE_ENC_KEY unset/);
	});
	it('returns stored ciphertext unchanged when decrypting without a key', async () => {
		expect(await decrypt_text({} as never, 'enc:AAAA')).toBe('enc:AAAA');
	});
```
Phase 2: watch them fail for the stated reason (DataError instead of named error; decrypt without key already returns stored but only if the cache is reset — without reset it returns ciphertext via the valid cached key, so the reset is what makes the first test meaningful). Phase 3: implement the aes_key guard + __reset_msg_crypto export. Phase 4: `pnpm vitest run src/lib/server/__tests__/msg_crypto.test.ts src/lib/server/__tests__/chat.test.ts` green, then `pnpm test`.
